title: Project and Task Management
version: 1.0.0
status: accepted
language: en

objective: >
  Extend the existing company-scoped project model with required project
  descriptions, a default per-task employee capacity, typed hierarchical tasks,
  and employee-managed task membership while preserving existing project
  allocation used by time tracking.

authority:
  preserve:
    - existing company-scoped RBAC
    - existing project soft-delete behavior
    - existing employee-project allocation used by project-filtered time punches
    - existing encrypted storage for project and task human-readable fields
  change:
    - project description becomes required and semantically non-empty at API boundary
    - project stores task_employee_limit with default 1 for legacy API compatibility
    - tasks and task employee memberships are introduced

authorization:
  managerial_roles:
    - manager
    - admin
    - super_admin
  employee_role:
    - employee
  rules:
    - company-scoped users with projects.create may create projects
    - company-scoped users with projects.update may update projects and their capacity
    - company-scoped users with projects.delete may soft-delete projects
    - company-scoped users with projects.assign may manage project allocations
    - company-scoped users with tasks.create may create tasks
    - company-scoped users with tasks.update may update tasks
    - authenticated users with an employee profile may join, leave, add, and remove task members
    - task membership operations cannot target employees outside the authenticated company
    - role and company identity are resolved from the authenticated backend context, never from client claims

project:
  required_fields:
    name:
      type: string
      constraints:
        - trimmed length 1..160
        - whitespace-only values rejected
    description:
      type: string
      constraints:
        - trimmed length 1..2000
        - whitespace-only values rejected
    task_employee_limit:
      type: integer
      constraints:
        - minimum 1
      default: 1
      rationale: preserve compatibility with existing project create/update clients that predate this field
  relationships:
    tasks: one_to_many
    employee_allocations: existing_many_to_many_preserved

task:
  required_fields:
    name:
      type: string
      constraints:
        - trimmed length 1..160
        - whitespace-only values rejected
    description:
      type: string
      constraints:
        - trimmed length 1..2000
        - whitespace-only values rejected
    type:
      enum:
        - bug
        - improvement
        - feature
  relationships:
    project: many_to_one_required
    parent: optional_many_to_one_self_reference
    employees: many_to_many
  hierarchy_invariants:
    - task cannot parent itself
    - parent must belong to the same project
    - assigning a parent cannot create a direct or indirect cycle

membership:
  operations:
    join_self:
      actor: authenticated employee
      result_when_new: 201
      result_when_duplicate: 200
    leave_self:
      actor: authenticated employee
      result: 204
      absent_membership: idempotent 204
    add_other:
      actor: authenticated employee
      result_when_new: 201
      result_when_duplicate: 200
    remove_other:
      actor: authenticated employee
      result: 204
      absent_membership: idempotent 204
  invariants:
    - employee and task belong to the same company through the task project
    - duplicate employee-task memberships are impossible
    - membership count never exceeds the project task_employee_limit
  capacity_failure:
    status: 409
    detail: Task employee capacity reached.
  concurrency:
    mechanism: >
      Serialize capacity-sensitive writes on the project. Databases that support
      SELECT FOR UPDATE lock the project row before checking/inserting memberships
      or lowering the limit. SQLite starts an explicit BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction
      before the same checks.
    invariant: count(task_employees for task) <= project.task_employee_limit

capacity_changes:
  increase: always allowed when positive
  decrease:
    allowed_when: new limit is greater than or equal to every existing task membership count
    rejected_when: any task currently has more members than the requested limit
    failure:
      status: 409
      detail: Project task employee limit is below current task membership.

persistence:
  projects:
    add_column:
      name: task_employee_limit
      type: integer
      nullable: false
      default: 1
  tasks:
    columns:
      - id
      - project_id
      - parent_task_id nullable
      - name_ciphertext
      - description_ciphertext
      - type
      - created_at
      - updated_at
    constraints:
      - project foreign key
      - parent task foreign key
      - self-parent check
  task_employees:
    primary_key:
      - task_id
      - employee_id
    foreign_keys:
      - task_id -> tasks.id
      - employee_id -> employees.id

api:
  project_changes:
    - POST /api/v1/projects accepts and returns taskEmployeeLimit
    - PUT/PATCH /api/v1/projects/{project_id} accepts and returns taskEmployeeLimit
  task_routes:
    - GET /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks
    - POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks
    - GET /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}
    - PUT /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}
    - PATCH /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}
    - GET /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}/members
    - POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}/members/me
    - DELETE /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}/members/me
    - POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}/members
    - DELETE /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}/members/{employee_id}

errors:
  validation: framework 422 response for invalid request payload
  unauthorized: 401
  forbidden: 403
  not_found: 404
  conflict: 409

compatibility:
  - existing project reads continue to work and gain taskEmployeeLimit
  - legacy rows that already have a null description are preserved on read; every create or update now requires a valid description, so no new null/empty description state can be persisted through the API
  - existing project creation clients may omit taskEmployeeLimit and receive default 1
  - existing project membership endpoints remain unchanged
  - existing time-clock project validation remains unchanged
  - the Flutter workspace exposes a Projects and Tasks screen through the existing navigation drawer
  - managerial actions are hidden for employee-only accounts while read and membership actions remain available according to backend permissions

acceptance_criteria:
  - managerial role can create a valid project and task
  - employee role cannot create, update, delete, or assign members to projects
  - employee role cannot create or update tasks
  - project and task reject missing, empty, or whitespace-only names/descriptions
  - project persists and returns taskEmployeeLimit
  - project can contain multiple tasks
  - task persists and returns type and optional parentTaskId
  - self-parent, cross-project parent, direct cycle, and indirect cycle are rejected
  - authenticated employee can join/leave a task and add/remove another company employee
  - duplicate membership is idempotent and consumes one slot
  - membership at exactly capacity is allowed and the next distinct membership is rejected
  - removing a member releases capacity
  - project capacity cannot be lowered below an existing task membership count
  - persistence schema upgrade adds task_employee_limit to legacy projects
  - existing project allocation and punch behavior remains green
  - Flutter contracts parse project/task responses and serialize create/update payloads
  - Flutter managers can create/edit projects and create/edit tasks from the workspace
  - Flutter employees can inspect tasks and join/leave task membership
  - Flutter task membership UI reflects project capacity and current members
